    "title": "How to watch March Madness. See NCAA basketball tournament schedule",
    "text": "Updated March 19, 2026, 12:08 p.m. ETIt’s that special time of year when brackets are busted, wings and pizzas are ordered, and people do whatever they can to get a quick glimpse of March Madness.The NCAA Tournament kicks off March 19 with 16 games taking place all over the country.Here's a look at how to get your fill of the Road to the Final Four.When do 2026 NCAA Tournament games start?The first game – TCU vs. Ohio State – will tip off at 12:15 p.m. Games will continue throughout the day.What channels are 2026 NCAA Tournament games on?The NCAA Tournament games will be shown on CBS, TBS, TNT and truTV.What's today's 2026 NCAA Tournament schedule?Here's a look at the NCAA Tournament schedule for March 19:TCU vs. Ohio State, 12:15 p.m., CBSTroy vs. Nebraska, 12:40 p.m., truTVSouth Florida vs. Louisville, 1:30 p.m., TNTHigh Point vs. Wisconsin, 1:50 p.m., TBSSiena vs. Duke, 2:50 p.m., CBSMcNeese State vs. Vanderbilt, 3:15 p.m., truTVNorth Dakota State vs. Michigan State, 4:05 p.m., TNTHawaii vs. Arkansas, 4:25 p.m., TBSVCU vs. North Carolina, 6:50 p.m., TNTMichigan vs. Howard, 7:10 p.m., CBSTexas vs. BYU, 7:25 p.m., TBSTexas A&M vs. St. Mary's, 7:35 p.m., truTVPenn vs. Illinois, 9:25 p.m., TNTSt. Louis vs. Georgia, 9:45 p.m., CBSKennesaw St. vs. Gonzaga, 10 p.m., TBSIdaho vs. Houston, 10:10 p.m., truTVStream select NCAA Tournament games with Fubo (free trial)How to stream March Madness games for freeFree March Madness streaming options: March Madness Live app | Fubo (free trial)There are two free streaming options for the Men's NCAA Tournament, aside from watching games that air nationally on CBS, which is a linear TV channel offering.The first option is Fubo, which carries CBS and offers a free trial to new subscribers. CBS will televise 21 games of this year's tournament.The other option is the March Madness Live app. Those who have CBS or one of the Turner Sports Networks channels — TBS, TNT and truTV — as part of their TV packages, they can sign into the March Madness Live app with their TV login credentials. The same will work for watching games on a laptop through the March Madness Live webpage on the NCAA website.March Madness streaming options: How to livestream NCAA Tournament gamesStreaming options: March Madness Live app | Sling TV | Fubo (free trial)In addition to the March Madness Live app and Fubo, Sling TV is another streaming option for March Madness games. Sling TV is a streaming option for games that will appear on TBS, TNT and truTV.TBS will televise 21 games, while truTV will air or simulcast a total of 24 games throughout the tournament, and TNT will air or simulcast a total of 15 games. The Final Four and national championship will also air on TBS, meaning Sling TV and the March Madness Live app are the only streaming options for those two rounds of the Men's NCAA Tournament.Watch NCAA Tournament game on SlingWhen does Villanova open 2026 NCAA Tournament play?Villanova will open its tournament play against Utah State at 4:10 p.m. March 20 in San Diego.The game will be broadcast on TNT.",
